From 5aa0a995b13d4304370b9a323a00c52de5e01a76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toby Smith <toby.smith@seluna.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:01:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input.<button>: each of the pad's buttons remappable; L2
 swaps, R2 fast-forwards, L3 blows

L3 was a third way into the in-game menu, beside F and HOME (#55), and no
button could be moved (#52). input.<button> (a b x y l r start select up
down left right l2 r2 l3 r3) now says what each does in a game: one of the
DS's buttons, or a job (menu, swap, save, load, ff, ffhold, screenshot,
blow, none). blow is the menu's Blow for as long as the button is held,
as SuperDrastic's blow key. The defaults are the pad as printed, L2 the
screens swapped, R2 fast-forward on and off, L3 a blow (it was the menu)
and R3 nothing (the RG DS Plus has none), as BananaOS sets SuperDrastic's.
F + a button, HOME and the menu's own keys never change, so no setting can
lock the menu away. The menu's Hotkeys page lists the buttons with a job.
