+| `kms.menu` | `on` | the in-game menu (src/menu.c: SuperDrastic's, in BananaOS's colours): F or HOME (and a button set to `menu`, `input.<button>`) pauses the game and opens it on both panels. Resume, Save and Load (8 slots with pictures; a load can be undone), Quick settings (volume, brightness, the microphone's meter and a blow), Restart game, Quit game. `kms.menu_test=<n>` opens it 3 s in, on the main page (1), Save (2), Load (3), Quick settings (4) or the quit question (5), for tests |
+| `input.<button>` | as the pad is printed; `input.l2` `swap`, `input.r2` `ff`, `input.l3` `blow`, `input.r3` `none` (the RG DS Plus has no R3) | what a button of the pad does in a game. `<button>`: `a` `b` `x` `y` `l` `r` `start` `select` `up` `down` `left` `right` `l2` `r2` `l3` `r3`. The value: one of the DS's buttons (`a` `b` `x` `y` `l` `r` `start` `select` `up` `down` `left` `right`; two buttons can be the same DS button) or a job: `menu` (the in-game menu, on release), `swap` (the screens, as F + SELECT, remembered for the game), `save` / `load` (slot 1, as F + R / F + L), `ff` (fast-forward on and off, as F + X), `ffhold` (fast-forward while held), `screenshot`, `blow` (the game hears a blow on the mic while it's held, the menu's Blow, the mic on or off), `none`. A keyboard's keys follow the button they stand for. F + a button, HOME and the menu's own keys never change, so no setting leaves you without the menu. A value it doesn't know is logged and the button keeps its own |
 | `kms.lowlat` | `off` | **Experimental.** `on`: low latency. Each frame is aimed at a vblank: the emulator's thread starts it as late as its measured time allows (its own work and the presenter's 2D wait and shader pass, each a decaying maximum, plus `kms.lowlat_pad_us`, plus up to 16 ms more after frames that showed late; never the time a frame waited for the panels), so the buttons are read as late as possible. Frames are held to their own vblank's window (never shown a refresh early) and up to three may wait, so a game slower than a refresh starts the next frame early instead of stuttering; the next frame always aims at the refresh after the last waiting one. Measured in 0.5.0 (agent-qa/LL2.md): 15-21 ms from a frame's start to the panels instead of 48-60, 0-3 repeats a minute in a Mario Kart DS race (single frames of 20-60 ms can't be hidden without buffering). cpugov uses a tighter step-down rule (`cpugov.tail` 0.8) and its own memory (`<rom>.<scale>.lowlat`). The game runs at the panels' rate (as `kms.pace=display`). `kms.lowlat_trace=<file>` writes each frame's times at the quit (also without `kms.lowlat`). `runahead1` / `runahead2`: that and run-ahead (`runahead`). A `[lowlat]` log line every 10 s |
 | `kms.lowlat_margin_us` | `1500` | with `kms.lowlat`: the deadline, this long before the earlier panel's vblank; +300 per commit that missed its vblank (at most 5000), back down after a clean 10 s |
 | `kms.lowlat_pad_us` | `1000` | with `kms.lowlat`: added to the frames' measured time when a frame is started |
diff --git a/bananads/src/frontend_kms.cpp b/bananads/src/frontend_kms.cpp
